# Copy to `.env.maestro` (gitignored via `.env.*`). Never commit real credentials.
#
# Two dedicated QA accounts on the Fluent API (see docs/guides/maestro.md):
#   Account A — translator shape (≥1 chapter assignment) → primary smokes
#   Account B — member-without-assignments (project membership, no assignee rows)
#               → empty-assignments + multi-account isolation
#
# Seed: both on the same QA project (e.g. Source Audio QA, BSB). Prefer distinct
# My Work labels when Account B ever gains assignments (isolation asserts).
#
# `scripts/maestro-test.sh` loads this file literally (no Bash expansion) when present.
# Role aliases below are optional; if set, they fill MAESTRO_EMAIL(_2) when those are empty.
# Or: `maestro test -e MAESTRO_EMAIL=... -e MAESTRO_PASSWORD=... .maestro/...`

# --- Account A: translator shape (canonical names used by flows / EAS secrets) ---
MAESTRO_EMAIL=
MAESTRO_PASSWORD=

# --- Account B: member-without-assignments ---
MAESTRO_EMAIL_2=
MAESTRO_PASSWORD_2=

# Optional aliases (same values as above — clearer local naming)
# MAESTRO_TRANSLATOR_EMAIL=
# MAESTRO_TRANSLATOR_PASSWORD=
# MAESTRO_PM_EMAIL=
# MAESTRO_PM_PASSWORD=

# API the Debug APK / Metro session should hit (must match your .env / Metro env).
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://dev.api.fluent.bible

# Local Debug + Metro only — suppresses Expo Dev Menu so it does not steal taps.
# Do NOT set on production / preview / nightly EAS profiles.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_E2E_MODE=1

# Launch mode: metro (default, Debug deep-link) | embedded (e2e-test / nightly APK)
# MAESTRO_LAUNCH_MODE=metro
# Optional override of the Dev Client deep-link (emulator → host via 10.0.2.2).
# Metro must listen on all interfaces (npm run maestro:metro — not --localhost).
# MAESTRO_DEV_CLIENT_URL=exp+fluent-mobile://expo-development-client/?url=http%3A%2F%2F10.0.2.2%3A8081%3FdisableOnboarding%3D1&disableFab=1&disableAutoLaunch=1
